Date:   Wed Jul 22 08:57:24 2026 +0000

    [kimi_k3] torchtitan engine: honor verl save_freq by setting checkpoint interval=1
    
    The engine built CheckpointManager.Config without an interval (torchtitan
    default 500) and save_checkpoint() never passed last_step, so the model save
    was gated by torchtitan's own 500-step interval, not verl's trainer.save_freq.
    Any run shorter than 500 steps (or whose save_freq did not land on a multiple
    of 500) silently wrote only dataloader state -- no model weights ever, the
    final step included. Set interval=1 so every save() call verl issues (already
    gated by save_freq) writes via the normal model+optimizer+extra DCP path.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016tHsrAsHfAP81fLpktESYP

diff --git a/verl/workers/engine/torchtitan/transformer_impl.py b/verl/workers/engine/torchtitan/transformer_impl.py
index 699946bb..40cced7a 100644
--- a/verl/workers/engine/torchtitan/transformer_impl.py
+++ b/verl/workers/engine/torchtitan/transformer_impl.py
@@ -152,6 +152,11 @@ class TorchTitanEngine(BaseEngine):
             initial_load_in_hf=True,
             initial_load_model_only=True,
             initial_load_path=model_config.path,
+            # verl's trainer.save_freq is the cadence authority and save() is
+            # only called on those steps; defer torchtitan's own interval to 1
+            # so every requested save writes (default 500 silently drops all
+            # saves in runs shorter than 500 / not multiples of it).
+            interval=1,
         )
         compile_config = CompileConfig(enable=self.engine_config.use_torch_compile)
         training_kwargs = {}
